## Final report

## Reviewed
`HEAD` (branch tip) @ `8bc7eded2f4b0ea4f940d16a09c118fcc7f4b536`, "pricing: simpler split_bill". One file changed: `tinyshop/pricing.py` (+3/−6). I got the diff with `git diff HEAD~1 HEAD`. The working tree was clean before I started.

## Findings (reproduced)
### F1: `split_bill` shares no longer add up to the total when it doesn't divide evenly
Where: tinyshop/pricing.py:5-6 (`share = round(total_cents / people)`; `return [share] * people`)
Command:
    python3 -c "from tinyshop.pricing import split_bill as s; r=s(100,3); print(r, sum(r))"
Output (exit 0):
    [33, 33, 33] 99
Rounding up also creates money:
    python3 -c "from tinyshop.pricing import split_bill as s; r=s(200,3); print(r, sum(r))"
Output (exit 0):
    [67, 67, 67] 201
Expected: `[34, 33, 33] 100`. The parent commit's version gives exactly that (I ran `HEAD~1:tinyshop/pricing.py` and got `[34, 33, 33] 100`, exit 0). The commit message says "Shares still add up to the total", and the docstring still says the same.
Fix: Put back the old version: `base, rem = divmod(total_cents, people)` and `return [base + 1 if i < rem else base for i in range(people)]`. Also add a test that checks `sum(split_bill(100, 3)) == 100`.

## Claims checked
| Claim | Source | Result | Evidence |
|---|---|---|---|
| "Shares still add up to the total." | Commit message | **refuted** | `split_bill(100,3)` → `[33, 33, 33] 99`; `split_bill(200,3)` → `[67, 67, 67] 201` |
| "Split a bill into whole-cent shares that add up to total_cents." | Docstring in the new code | **refuted** | Same output as above |
| Project tests pass | Implied | confirmed, but they don't cover this | `python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -t .` → `Ran 5 tests in 0.000s` / `OK`, exit 0. `tests/test_pricing.py` only tests an even split (`900, 3`) and `people=0`, so it can't catch F1. |

